    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for July 21st hinges on exploiting favorable platoon splits and high-leverage SP matchups, with **Bryce Harper** (71.47) and **Taylor Ward** (66.37) headlining our daily output. **Bryce Harper** draws a prime opportunity against Wrobleski, bolstered by favorable winds and an advantageous matchup against a left-handed arm, while **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive +10% boost for hitting atop the order against Ed Rivera. **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.93) is our dark horse play today; he faces the highest-ERA pitcher on our radar in Avila (4.96 xERA), and his ability to maximize the platoon advantage against a right-hander makes him an essential start despite his lower-tier power profile. **Gleyber Torres** (64.48) and **Jonathan Aranda** (60.01) also provide high-floor production, with **Jonathan Aranda**\u2019s +12% platoon edge helping him weather the challenge of facing a high-caliber arm in Gausman.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Lawrence Butler** (46.39) and **JJ Bleday** (46.11), both of whom provided respectable base projections but failed to crack the top 11. **Lawrence Butler** was ultimately sidelined by a unfavorable platoon split against Kohl Drake, further exacerbated by a projected #8 spot in the lineup that cannibalized his fantasy ceiling. While **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert** possess lower base floors, their specific alignment against L\u00f3pez and Avila offered higher upside for counting stats. Note the heightened risk surrounding **Gleyber Torres**; despite his strong 64.48 score, the 41% rain risk at the stadium warrants close monitoring, as a delay or cancellation could derail one of our most efficient middle-infield options. We are also managing the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Geraldo Perdomo**, whose official lineup confirmations remain pending; should they drop in the order, their efficiency scores will adjust, but for now, their current projections justify their spots. Stay alert to any late-breaking roster news for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL.",
